i2c_hid: support EXTENDED_IRQ as input-ready line

Some trackpads (Dell XPS 15 9560) put an Extended IRQ resource in
_CRS instead of a GPIO interrupt. InputReadyLine only looked for the
GPIO type, so Init failed, fInputReady stayed NULL, and the driver
re-read the input register forever.

Add a second walker for ACPI_RESOURCE_TYPE_EXTENDED_IRQ. When one is
found, install an interrupt handler that sets a flag. IsAsserted
returns and clears that flag. The existing loop in MaybeScheduleTransfer
then only reads when a report is actually ready.

The GPIO pad path is unchanged.

See https://github.com/RenkuOS/Source/issues/702
